the exp_r26 artifact, in THIS tokenizer's pieces:
  r_41027    4 tokens: ['r', '_', '410', '27']
  damuzo     3 tokens: ['dam', 'uz', 'o']
  exp_r26's 5.7x swing was measured on the STAND-IN's vocabulary, not this
  one, so the artifact is not automatically ours. Run both (--gguf) before
  claiming it transfers: measured 2026-09-15, both split `r_41027` into
  ['r', '_', '410', '27'] and both fragment role identifiers to ~8 tokens,
  so it does transfer -- and the repo's own 128k is slightly WORSE than the
  stand-in (8.67 vs 7.83 mean tokens per role).
  Each token is a decode step the model can fumble. Fragmentation is what
  makes that possible; a grammar mask (WO-2.2) is what makes it impossible.

